    "note": "Q613037 identifies Temple of Edfu. Standard PMTiles building52776572243683 supplies its eight-point perimeter and open inner court; five independent roof-range controls and the southern building with fifteen parts retain their own positions. The593-by258m archaeological-site boundary is not the temple footprint. Raw+X east/+Z south and heading0 preserve the signed south-facing pylon front,2.08 degrees west of south. Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged161-square/6m standard DEM. Cross-axis medians set a graded visualization floor; both occupied compounds retain complete floors in every level. Local ground openings and perimeter joins remain bounded to those compounds. Loading replaces22 mapped temple/column records and preserves26 independent buildings in the960m tile exactly;27 independent records are preserved across the larger extract. No water is present in this local extract. Failure retains all48 native tile buildings and original ground; eviction restores ground and frees all geometry. A synthetic64m partial tile verifies clipping and lifecycle only. It exposes the existing terrain-excavation sky-sliver limitation at temporary clipped boundaries; full-site contact does not approve those temporary edges. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
